{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1431742-is-minds-eye-theatre-canon-to-the-tabletop-lore","id":1431742,"title":"is minds eye theatre canon to the tabletop lore?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-01-10T12:47:04-08:00","id":1431742,"title":"is minds eye theatre canon to the tabletop lore?","content":"I'm interested in knowing, are the mind's eye theatre book's canon to the tabletop, or do they change a lot of what's in the tabletop?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26129-harbinger1999","name":"Harbinger1999","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26129_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-10T12:55:36-08:00","id":1431744,"title":"","content":"They share canon up to the appearance of the Red Star and the Week of Nightmares in the run-up to Gehenna.<br /> <br /> After that point, MET canon goes in one direction and V5 goes in another. (V20 is specifically designed to be metaplot-neutral so it's hard to say that it has &quot;canon&quot; as such).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/100-jezmiller","name":"JezMiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-10T17:17:07-08:00","id":1431772,"title":"","content":"No I think they Alternate cannons. Like some parts of the setting that work will in Tabletop wouldn\u2019t go on will in LARP and vice versa so MET changes the lore a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-10T18:00:38-08:00","id":1431776,"title":"","content":"I think that MET broadly followed the same meta plot and backstory elements when they were still published by White Wolf. The writers and developers involved were basically the same as the tabletop game. When By Night Studios took up the license, they may have deviated a bit because the writing team were different, but would have still been regulated by the terms of the license I\u2019d imagine. I think V5 moved the timeline and meta plot forward a bit, and came out a few years after the MET: VTM book was released, so that could be different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-10T18:07:17-08:00","id":1431777,"title":"","content":"The history of the Gangrel clearly diverges, and that's just off the top of my head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-11T01:39:54-08:00","id":1431805,"title":"","content":"V5 builds on metaplot established and expanded in V20 rather than the latest versions of MET.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-11T23:20:01-08:00","id":1431928,"title":"","content":"Yeah the latest MET version seems like it differed drastically from how V20 and V5 went with things. Doesn't mean its 100% incompatible, but might require kludging (then again that's true of most things in the ST system if you want to throw them together. It's very lose with canon even if it tries to apply a coherent continuity - assuming one treats those as separate things. Which I do.) <br /> The earlier iterations I think were more closely tied together but you still could have narrative differences as well as mechanical ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-13T06:46:19-08:00","id":1432077,"title":"","content":"MET has some cool ideas to scavenge if you care to. They've established who the Sabbat's previous regents before Gorchist were, which canon never did.<br /> <br /> I also like Temoch the Jackal a lot as the sect's current regent. He's the kind of diablerist zealot who feels very appropriate to its new incarnation.<br /> <br /> V20/V5 has yet to provide information on several of its justicars, so I just use MET's instead. There are a couple others who I prefer for the job. (Theo Bell exempted...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-13T12:50:53-08:00","id":1432110,"title":"","content":"MET always felt like it was 'truer' to creator's intent for the Storyteller system than the tabletop was, since it was more about role-playing and narrative and less about game mechanics. I doa gree they can have interesting ideas (partly because they take a different approach from tabletop) but it can be 'interesting' to adapt them (I still consider V5 to be a fusion of MET and tabletop for that reason.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-13T14:13:00-08:00","id":1432124,"title":"","content":"MET can never live up to the power of imagination, and has so many crutches as a result.<br /> I remember when 5th edition was announced, the official website suggested werewolves have dayjobs as the rule rather than the exception, which is Heresy. The whole deal with werewolves is that they live in the sticks with their cult communes and can't deal with normal people because of all that Rage but there we were with an official website using what I assume to be a LARP convention and applying it to the tabletop.<br /> <br /> V5 is more MET friendly. IE physical disciplines do very specific things rather than provide overall improvements, and Dominate was stripped down so that you can't bully RL people so cleverly.<br /> <br /> Obviously, I'm no great knowledge on the subject because I'm not terribly familiar with actual MET play (I've read some rules and have my prejudices) but they're very different and you should never ever under any circumstances dictate canon for such a rich IP through LARP of all mediums.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-13T14:33:01-08:00","id":1432128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1431742-is-minds-eye-theatre-canon-to-the-tabletop-lore?p=1432124#post1432124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V5 is more MET friendly. IE physical disciplines do very specific things rather than provide overall improvements, and Dominate waswas stripped down so that you can't bully RL people so cleverly.<br /> <br /> Obviously, I'm no great knowledge on the subject because I'm not terribly familiar with actual MET play (I've read some rules and have my prejudices) but they're very different and you should never ever under any circumstances dictate canon for such a rich IP through LARP of all mediums.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is possibly the first post I\u2019ve read of yours where I find myself in some agreement. The way in which V5 was written, with the increased emphasis on diceless play actually lends itself better to live-action play than the current MET books.<br /> <br /> When the MET games first came out in 1993, noting that live action play had already been a part of the tabletop rules too, the new game system was possibly one of the most interesting things about it. Things like spending traits on contests between characters to determine outcomes, in my view, actually laid a lot of groundwork towards a lot of later \u2018narrative\u2019 games. Rock-Paper-Scissors was a bit different, but intuitive, and the smaller books managed to condense the lore down into an easily digestible way, while being portable enough to carry around a LARP.<br /> <br /> The current By Night books, by contrast are massive beyond comprehension - and lose some of their functionality because of it. Even if you use an electronic device, searching a 500+ page book isn\u2019t easy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-19T18:20:39-08:00","id":1531160,"title":"","content":"It is a very little thing, and hardly a canon thing<br /> But I love the Anarch positions they have, for is not just an emulation of the other sects, but offices that seem to help out in building an Anarch (and possibly Anarchist) society, instead of always going neofeudal-mobster Baron style. Lots of these tiny, mostly out of mechanizing the society and politics of vampire features, I love in MET.<br /> <br /> Before V5 did the Family Reunion, and gave some true core and heft to a true Clan of Death, I liked the alliance between the Setites and Giovanni (the pact of las vegas I think?)<br /> <br /> I can't think of much right now, or many examples really, but there truly are some cool recontextualization of events through MET, that in the tabletop are treated as anything... Besides, I think their canon is responsible for like 1/4th of the Treaties and Pacts we have in lore. Either way, their focus on social and political aspects are great!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}